WEBVTT

00:13.805 --> 00:17.726
Weather Forecast!

00:20.270 --> 00:21.813
When did you take it from me?

00:21.896 --> 00:24.441
Was it when Jolyne blasted you?

00:24.524 --> 00:25.942
Give it back immediately.

00:26.025 --> 00:27.819
It belongs to me.

00:27.902 --> 00:30.864
You don't understand what you're doing.

00:30.947 --> 00:33.575
He's starting to remember.

00:33.658 --> 00:35.326
Look, he's here.

00:37.954 --> 00:41.958
Rainbows. There are rainbows!
The devil's rainbows!

00:42.042 --> 00:43.710
It's Heavy Forecast!

00:46.796 --> 00:49.382
Weather, what's the matter?

00:49.883 --> 00:51.009
What are you doing?

00:56.264 --> 00:58.016
What's your problem, punk?

00:58.099 --> 01:00.852
I was sitting here first.

01:00.935 --> 01:04.522
Don't touch me, I'll kill you!

01:10.320 --> 01:13.782
Hey! You can't take
an injured person's seat--

01:15.075 --> 01:17.494
Stop fussing.

01:17.577 --> 01:20.455
You want him to sit, do you?

01:23.416 --> 01:26.336
He can sit on you then.

01:29.047 --> 01:31.257
Weather! What are you doing?

01:31.341 --> 01:32.675
He's not an enemy!

01:32.759 --> 01:34.719
He's just a nurse!

01:38.014 --> 01:41.810
Now, sit all you want, crutch guy.

01:43.269 --> 01:45.021
I've never felt better.

01:47.357 --> 01:49.317
Wait up!

01:49.400 --> 01:51.319
Weather, where do you think you're going?

01:52.612 --> 01:55.490
Weather? Don't Weather me.

01:55.573 --> 01:57.784
So I go by Weather Forecast now.

01:59.494 --> 02:02.247
Not a bad name.

02:04.833 --> 02:06.960
What happened to him?

02:07.043 --> 02:08.211
It's as if…

02:09.129 --> 02:10.713
he's gained an entirely new personality!

03:42.639 --> 03:47.810
EPISODE 30: HEAVY FORECAST (1)

03:47.894 --> 03:49.062
Rainbows!

03:50.146 --> 03:52.565
Rainbows are closing in on us!

03:55.485 --> 03:58.154
Jolyne, we have no time to waste!

03:58.238 --> 03:59.322
This looks serious!

04:00.323 --> 04:01.658
It's over!

04:01.741 --> 04:03.493
Meet your end!

04:09.666 --> 04:12.961
- What the hell?
- Ermes?

04:14.921 --> 04:16.923
What just happened?

04:17.006 --> 04:19.676
- Was it an illusion?
- This is bad.

04:19.759 --> 04:23.137
Your life is in danger, but so is mine.

04:23.221 --> 04:25.306
You untied yourself.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.558
I'm warning you.

04:27.642 --> 04:29.894
Don't touch those rainbows.

04:29.978 --> 04:34.107
Those are Weather Forecast's rainbows
Father Pucchi sealed up!

04:34.190 --> 04:37.652
Weather Forecast's Stand ability
controls the weather.

04:38.820 --> 04:40.822
Do you understand what this means?

04:40.905 --> 04:45.910
With his memory restored,
he can even destroy the ozone layer.

04:46.452 --> 04:49.580
The ozone is even higher than the sky.

04:49.664 --> 04:52.500
What could come
from messing with the ozone?

04:53.126 --> 04:55.670
I can only say that it won't end well,

04:55.753 --> 04:57.380
but we're all in danger.

04:57.463 --> 04:59.841
The survival of humanity is at stake!

05:00.383 --> 05:01.843
It was a risky sacrifice,

05:01.926 --> 05:05.763
but I used Weather Forecast
to save my skin!

05:05.847 --> 05:09.726
What did the ozone do to my Smack?

05:09.809 --> 05:14.397
Answer me. Do these rainbows mean
that Weather's memory is back?

05:15.148 --> 05:17.066
The rainbows come out
from his subconscious.

05:18.901 --> 05:22.405
Weather Forecast's Stand
has an automatic attack.

05:22.488 --> 05:25.116
The weather is a complex phenomenon.

05:25.199 --> 05:28.786
His ability manifests in ways
he doesn't realize.

05:30.580 --> 05:34.125
His memory should never
have been returned to him.

05:34.208 --> 05:35.209
I'll tell you this.

05:35.710 --> 05:38.629
To stop the rainbows,
you must kill Weather,

05:38.713 --> 05:41.841
or extract his memory again.

05:42.508 --> 05:46.637
Jolyne, can you kill Weather?

05:46.721 --> 05:50.600
If not, then humanity may end
before the new moon.

05:52.393 --> 05:56.105
Though, I won't end here.

05:58.816 --> 06:01.486
You shouldn't let Versus escape.

06:04.530 --> 06:06.074
Versus fled, Jolyne!

06:09.702 --> 06:11.412
There are two women here!

06:11.496 --> 06:13.498
- Officer!
- Officer!

06:13.581 --> 06:15.041
This is…

06:15.124 --> 06:16.542
Was the hole this shallow?

06:16.626 --> 06:19.754
He deactivated Netherworld and took off!

06:23.633 --> 06:24.717
Where did they go?

06:24.801 --> 06:26.427
Did you see two men running off?

06:26.511 --> 06:27.595
Which way did they go?

06:27.678 --> 06:29.347
Before we get to that,

06:29.430 --> 06:31.015
I've seen your faces…

06:31.099 --> 06:32.809
On a wanted fugitives list!

06:34.644 --> 06:36.437
Rainbows. Just what is going on?

06:37.021 --> 06:38.523
It's everywhere!

06:38.606 --> 06:39.524
Hey!

06:43.027 --> 06:44.153
What's going on?

06:44.237 --> 06:45.404
You two!

06:45.488 --> 06:47.406
You're the escaped convicts!

06:55.873 --> 06:59.043
Don't go anywhere!

06:59.127 --> 07:02.088
Get over here!

07:03.381 --> 07:07.218
- Don't touch the rainbows!
- Stay away from them!

07:08.302 --> 07:09.720
Jolyne!

07:18.062 --> 07:21.482
What do we do?

07:21.566 --> 07:24.902
This is terrible!

07:27.155 --> 07:30.158
What is going on?

07:30.241 --> 07:33.077
Anyone who touches a rainbow
secretes snails!

07:33.744 --> 07:37.498
I've seen Weather rain down
frogs in a storm.

07:38.082 --> 07:40.835
But these snails are entirely different.

07:40.918 --> 07:43.212
How does this phenomenon relate
to Weather Forecast

07:43.296 --> 07:45.798
and his ability to manipulate the weather?

07:46.299 --> 07:47.133
Not only that,

07:48.176 --> 07:52.513
once infected by the snails,
people are losing their minds. 

07:52.597 --> 07:55.057
You can't run!

08:06.152 --> 08:07.403
What is going on?

08:07.487 --> 08:08.404
Ermes!

08:11.532 --> 08:13.618
Jolyne! Are you okay?

08:14.368 --> 08:15.286
Yeah.

08:16.454 --> 08:17.622
Ermes.

08:17.705 --> 08:20.625
Compared to normal people,
Stand Users may have a tolerance

08:20.708 --> 08:22.960
to this kind of phenomenon.

08:23.044 --> 08:24.962
So Jolyne,

08:25.046 --> 08:27.048
who should we target?

08:27.131 --> 08:29.467
Who do we need to defeat?

08:29.550 --> 08:31.469
Is Weather Forecast an enemy,

08:32.011 --> 08:35.264
or do we keep going after the priest?

08:35.348 --> 08:37.558
Tell me, who do we get rid of?

08:40.019 --> 08:44.815
Weather Forecast, with his memories,
is our enemy!

08:44.899 --> 08:47.944
No! Weather Forecast is our ally.

08:48.027 --> 08:49.654
He's not our enemy!

08:49.737 --> 08:51.280
We have to find Versus.

08:51.364 --> 08:53.074
Just like the priest said,

08:53.157 --> 08:55.159
we can't let Versus go free.

08:55.826 --> 08:58.496
His ability is to excavate memories.

08:58.579 --> 09:01.082
Maybe we can unearth
Weather's memory disc,

09:01.165 --> 09:03.584
and stop this bizarre phenomenon.

09:03.668 --> 09:05.044
I like your line of thinking.

09:05.127 --> 09:06.379
But first,

09:06.921 --> 09:09.215
we need to get out of this hospital!

09:19.725 --> 09:22.353
Hey! Where are you headed, Weather?

09:22.436 --> 09:25.022
Is that where Jolyne is?

09:25.648 --> 09:26.482
Tell me!

09:27.275 --> 09:28.568
Shit.

09:31.529 --> 09:33.072
I want it.

09:33.155 --> 09:35.741
I want that power.

09:35.825 --> 09:38.035
I need to get it before the priest!

09:38.119 --> 09:39.996
The power to attain heaven.

09:40.079 --> 09:42.582
I want to live a good life!

09:42.665 --> 09:46.502
What should be my next course of action?

09:46.586 --> 09:48.671
Netherworld!

09:49.380 --> 09:50.548
Found it.

09:50.631 --> 09:54.594
The memory of the ground
when these two arrived at the hospital.

09:54.677 --> 09:55.678
Ermes.

09:56.262 --> 10:00.182
Now is our chance,
when we go after Father Pucchi.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.183
So don't worry.

10:01.267 --> 10:02.101
What?

10:02.602 --> 10:05.605
My father's disc can be sent
to the Speedwagon Foundation,

10:05.688 --> 10:09.317
while we have Father Pucchi's attention.

10:09.400 --> 10:11.569
Emporio will not fail.

10:11.652 --> 10:14.238
Father will finally come back to us.

10:14.864 --> 10:19.785
So Emporio is the ally's name
whom Jolyne was calling.

10:19.869 --> 10:21.454
I have to find him.

10:22.038 --> 10:24.749
It's someone
even the priest wasn't aware of.

10:25.333 --> 10:27.627
I don't know what Emporio looks like,

10:27.710 --> 10:29.420
since I haven't dug up a memory of him.

10:29.503 --> 10:31.172
But with all this commotion going on,

10:31.756 --> 10:34.967
Jotaro Kujo's disc must still be with him.

10:35.051 --> 10:37.261
He hasn't gotten it to this foundation.

10:37.803 --> 10:41.974
Jotaro's disc gave the priest
the idea of getting into heaven.

10:42.975 --> 10:44.852
If I get a hold of that disc,

10:44.935 --> 10:46.729
even I can go to heaven!

10:46.812 --> 10:48.939
The rainbows are my chance!

10:49.023 --> 10:52.943
Jotaro's disc belongs to me!

10:55.071 --> 10:59.241
These snails are multiplying so fast,
they've covered the entire floor!

10:59.325 --> 11:02.745
They won't stop reproducing!

11:02.828 --> 11:05.539
Snails are asexual.

11:05.623 --> 11:08.501
They pierce each other with love darts.

11:08.584 --> 11:11.253
Both snails then give birth
to dozens of baby snails!

11:11.337 --> 11:13.172
Good grief.

11:13.255 --> 11:16.175
They have sex with anything
that comes their way?

11:16.258 --> 11:21.347
I'm a bit jealous… I mean, that's creepy.

11:24.725 --> 11:26.560
- Ermes!
- Got it.

11:26.644 --> 11:27.520
Smack!

11:30.272 --> 11:31.941
Stone Ocean!

11:39.281 --> 11:41.450
No User has two Stands.

11:41.534 --> 11:45.037
Weather Forecast can only
control the weather.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.039
But this is entirely different.

11:47.540 --> 11:50.000
Just what is going on?

11:55.214 --> 11:56.966
STAND NAME: WEATHER FORECAST
STAND MASTER: WEATHER FORECAST

11:58.008 --> 12:00.719
Back when life first began to emerge
in the form of plants,

12:00.803 --> 12:04.515
oxygen began to form.

12:05.516 --> 12:07.351
Oxygen is made up of O2,

12:07.435 --> 12:11.105
which bonds with a third oxygen molecule.

12:11.188 --> 12:13.774
Ozone consists of O3 molecules.

12:14.275 --> 12:17.862
The ozonosphere occurs
at altitudes of 20 kilometers

12:17.945 --> 12:20.865
to 25 kilometers.

12:22.032 --> 12:25.786
If this ozone layer
were compromised in any way,

12:25.870 --> 12:28.956
what would become of life on Earth?

12:29.790 --> 12:33.711
Humans cannot predict
irregularities in weather patterns.

12:33.794 --> 12:37.840
We can only analyze past weather patterns

12:37.923 --> 12:40.009
collected over decades.

12:43.762 --> 12:45.306
I'm going ahead!

12:45.389 --> 12:47.933
Where is he? He has to be here.

12:48.017 --> 12:49.810
He must be close by.

12:49.894 --> 12:52.646
I'll find him and seize the disc,

12:53.481 --> 12:56.066
before it's handed to that foundation!

12:57.026 --> 12:59.195
He'll probably head to the hospital

12:59.278 --> 13:02.948
because he won't abandon Jolyne!

13:03.532 --> 13:06.744
The one who goes in to find Jolyne
must be Emporio!

13:06.827 --> 13:09.788
He'll be the one who's going
opposite everyone else.

13:10.748 --> 13:13.542
Dammit! I refuse to lose!

13:13.626 --> 13:16.170
I'm going to live a happy life!

13:18.589 --> 13:21.342
Jolyne, I wish I could help.

13:21.425 --> 13:22.426
But…

13:23.010 --> 13:26.305
I have to go deliver this disc
to the Foundation's messenger!

13:27.223 --> 13:32.353
I promised Jolyne to get
her father's disc to the Foundation.

13:32.436 --> 13:36.565
The Foundation rep said
to meet in five minutes!

13:37.191 --> 13:39.109
Dammit!

13:39.860 --> 13:41.612
What the hell?

13:41.695 --> 13:44.406
No one is headed toward the hospital!

13:44.907 --> 13:46.492
He has to be in the area.

13:46.575 --> 13:48.953
I just know it!

14:01.257 --> 14:03.175
Hello? Jolyne?

14:04.802 --> 14:05.636
Hello?

14:15.938 --> 14:17.690
I got you now.

14:17.773 --> 14:21.944
Thanks, Netherworld.
The earth never fails me.

14:22.027 --> 14:25.614
The memory of Jolyne had his number!

14:26.198 --> 14:29.118
Emporio relayed the survivors'
seat numbers to Jolyne

14:29.201 --> 14:31.287
using his cell phone!

14:31.370 --> 14:36.250
Meaning, Jolyne knows his cell number!

14:37.167 --> 14:39.837
Who would've thought
Emporio was a little boy?

14:41.088 --> 14:45.092
Even the priest
didn't know about this kid.

14:50.389 --> 14:53.350
What's this? He doesn't have the disc.

14:53.976 --> 14:57.021
Moreover, he doesn't have his
phone either.

14:57.605 --> 14:58.939
He had it a moment ago!

14:59.690 --> 15:01.442
Hold on, I need to keep my head cool.

15:01.942 --> 15:04.653
I can excavate to learn
what he did with the disc.

15:04.737 --> 15:06.113
I can watch him put it away!

15:06.739 --> 15:08.908
Oh, shit.

15:08.991 --> 15:09.992
It's them!

15:17.750 --> 15:20.961
- Are you sure he came this way, Jolyne?
- Yeah.

15:21.045 --> 15:22.922
I feel his presence over here.

15:23.005 --> 15:27.092
I'm sure I saw Emporio going this way.

15:28.093 --> 15:30.387
Wait, do you think he's after Emporio?

15:30.471 --> 15:31.972
Impossible.

15:32.056 --> 15:35.643
Even the priest doesn't know
about Emporio, so how can Versus know?

15:36.936 --> 15:39.313
- That's…
- Emporio!

15:44.777 --> 15:46.445
Watch out! Jump!

15:53.827 --> 15:55.329
Disgusting!

15:56.580 --> 15:58.666
These are real, all right.

15:58.749 --> 15:59.792
Not illusions.

16:00.501 --> 16:03.128
So slimy and gross.

16:12.054 --> 16:12.888
Ermes!

16:18.268 --> 16:20.479
Jolyne, go without me.

16:20.562 --> 16:22.272
Go find Emporio!

16:22.356 --> 16:25.275
That was definitely him getting dragged.

16:25.359 --> 16:28.988
I don't know how he found out,
but Versus is after Emporio.

16:30.072 --> 16:31.490
Stone Ocean!

16:35.911 --> 16:37.079
Dammit.

16:37.162 --> 16:38.288
My rope!

16:38.372 --> 16:40.791
My movements are slowed to snail's pace!

16:41.875 --> 16:43.127
Emporio!

16:43.210 --> 16:46.130
If you can hear me, pull on my rope!
Grab onto it!

16:47.381 --> 16:49.174
Forty-five, sixty!

16:49.758 --> 16:50.926
Hut!

16:56.056 --> 16:57.516
Jolyne!

16:58.517 --> 17:00.019
This is Florida.

17:00.102 --> 17:02.896
I dug up memories about the Superbowl.

17:02.980 --> 17:04.481
Jolyne Cujoh,

17:04.565 --> 17:08.110
the quarterback will carry you
all the way to the touchdown line.

17:08.193 --> 17:09.361
My thread!

17:09.445 --> 17:11.739
You are too slow to do anything.

17:11.822 --> 17:15.159
Bye. You're too far away now.

17:15.242 --> 17:18.370
Yikes, I shouldn't touch these snails.

17:19.955 --> 17:21.415
I wasn't wrong.

17:21.498 --> 17:25.544
He had Jotaro's disc just moments ago.

17:26.086 --> 17:29.757
A second later,
his disc suddenly disappears.

17:29.840 --> 17:32.259
He must have used his Stand ability.

17:32.342 --> 17:36.764
He's able to stash things
with his ability.

17:36.847 --> 17:39.975
Then where did he put the disc?

17:40.059 --> 17:41.435
I should check again.

17:43.729 --> 17:44.605
What?

17:45.522 --> 17:47.066
Where's Jolyne?

17:47.149 --> 17:49.818
She's a snail. She can't move quickly!

18:01.497 --> 18:04.208
Unbelievable, she caught up to him.

18:04.291 --> 18:05.501
She rolled over!

18:06.085 --> 18:08.796
She squeezed into a streetlight pole
that broke in half.

18:08.879 --> 18:13.217
Now that her body has turned gooey,
she can easily fit in a metal pole!

18:15.219 --> 18:17.387
Netherworld!

18:18.597 --> 18:20.974
I didn't expect you to roll yourself over,

18:21.058 --> 18:22.810
but this doesn't change a thing.

18:22.893 --> 18:25.604
You are still powerless
against my Netherworld!

18:27.564 --> 18:29.691
I excavated a certain memory.

18:29.775 --> 18:32.736
Memory of ocean water
evaporating and leaving salt!

18:33.320 --> 18:37.783
Snails and slugs can't stand salt!

18:41.787 --> 18:42.955
What?

18:47.960 --> 18:49.670
Shit, where is it?

18:50.295 --> 18:53.006
I know you have the disc somewhere.

18:53.090 --> 18:54.633
You've hidden it somewhere.

18:54.716 --> 18:57.094
Where did you stash it?

19:03.475 --> 19:07.020
I see, so our Stands work similarly.

19:07.104 --> 19:10.858
His Stand controls
the memories of objects.

19:11.483 --> 19:13.193
I did it!

19:13.277 --> 19:15.195
I found Jotaro's memory disc!

19:15.279 --> 19:16.655
It's mine now!

19:16.738 --> 19:18.866
I win!

19:18.949 --> 19:21.034
And now, finally,

19:21.118 --> 19:24.037
I'm a step closer to the heaven
that priest is after!

19:24.121 --> 19:25.998
Jolyne!

19:26.790 --> 19:28.584
I'm sorry, Emporio.

19:29.084 --> 19:31.378
I used you as bait.

19:31.879 --> 19:33.964
You touched me,

19:34.548 --> 19:37.259
and he touched you.

19:37.342 --> 19:40.220
Feeling the sensation… All at once…

19:42.764 --> 19:45.601
I'm so slow!

19:58.530 --> 20:00.991
Damn right, he's ours now!

20:01.074 --> 20:02.659
Nice going, Jolyne!

20:07.414 --> 20:08.498
Emporio.

20:11.501 --> 20:12.502
It's no use.

20:12.586 --> 20:16.298
The Speedwagon Foundation's messenger
can't enter the city limits.

20:16.381 --> 20:17.883
He's just standing by.

20:17.966 --> 20:19.134
Is that right?

20:21.929 --> 20:23.805
Nicely done.

20:23.889 --> 20:25.390
You got it, carjacker.

20:25.474 --> 20:27.601
Let me set things straight.

20:27.684 --> 20:30.187
I've never stolen a car.

20:30.270 --> 20:31.939
I'm messing with you.

20:32.481 --> 20:33.982
You're coming with us.

20:34.608 --> 20:37.277
Don't even think about running again.

20:37.361 --> 20:39.446
I know.

20:44.076 --> 20:44.952
What's this?

20:45.035 --> 20:48.455
Are these the driver's shells?

20:48.538 --> 20:51.166
But why just shells?

20:53.293 --> 20:54.628
Shells here too.

20:55.837 --> 20:59.466
Okay, I'm catching on.

21:01.802 --> 21:07.933
I don't know what Weather did
to transform people into snails.

21:08.016 --> 21:11.561
But I do know what lies ahead of us.

21:12.271 --> 21:16.108
The snails' natural enemies
which feed on them.

21:17.526 --> 21:19.778
Snails can only move slowly,

21:19.861 --> 21:22.197
so they often die like this.

21:22.281 --> 21:25.784
These beetles stick their heads
inside the shells

21:25.867 --> 21:28.370
and devour the snails!

21:29.079 --> 21:31.290
That's why these beetles are called
snail eaters!

21:31.373 --> 21:33.875
These buggers!

21:40.257 --> 21:41.425
Hey Weather!

21:41.508 --> 21:43.552
I said wait up! Hey!

21:45.470 --> 21:46.888
What's going on?

21:46.972 --> 21:48.849
Did you cause this?

21:48.932 --> 21:52.352
Weather! What have you done?

21:53.478 --> 21:56.606
Silence, Anastasia.

21:57.733 --> 22:00.652
He is closing in on us.

22:01.778 --> 22:04.448
He is within a 20-meter radius.

22:05.282 --> 22:07.451
Him? You mean, Father Pucchi?

22:08.076 --> 22:09.036
He's here.

22:09.786 --> 22:12.372
My sole purpose in life

22:12.456 --> 22:14.708
is to settle my score with him.

23:41.294 --> 23:46.299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
